drydock-hail-service = Drydock services

drydock-hail-greeting-1 = { $location }, { $name } speaking. Go ahead, { $ship }.
drydock-hail-greeting-2 = This is { $name } at { $location }. Reading you, { $ship }.
drydock-hail-greeting-3 = { $location } dockmaster. What do you need, { $ship }?

drydock-hail-offer = Open drydock services and tell me what she needs. I'll find a berth.
drydock-hail-booked = Berth { $berth } is booked for you. Hold still there and work starts.
drydock-hail-working = Berth { $berth } is working on your ship, { $minutes } min left.

drydock-dockmaster-greeting = Dockmaster's desk. What do you need?
drydock-dockmaster-farewell = Mind the cranes.
drydock-dockmaster-prompt-how = How does the drydock work?
drydock-dockmaster-response-how = Hail me or use the console at my desk and I'll book a berth that fits. Follow the green lights in and hold still. You pay when the cranes start, and anything they don't finish or can't reach is refunded.
drydock-dockmaster-prompt-hail = Do I have to come in person?
drydock-dockmaster-response-hail = Not at all. Hail me from your helm and pick drydock services.
drydock-dockmaster-prompt-who = Who are you?
drydock-dockmaster-response-who = Hammer Ironstrike, dockmaster of Anvilhold. Forty years swinging cranes and I've not dropped a hull yet.
